 "text": "Hey, good to hear from you. How are you doing? Not exactly. It' called century because it's one hundred miles, not one hour. It' a popular distance for bike riders. Roughly twenty hours, at average speed of twenty miles an hour. You' need breaks for food and changes of scenery. It is, and it' worth doing at a weekend with nobody around to tell you to stop. Start, and take lots of small breaks. Set a time goal and try to beat it. It gives you something to aim at and makes the day feel more structured. Start with a few shorter rides a week, building up to about hour before the big day. Mix it up with some hills and traffic too, so you're as ready as you can get.",
